#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""
CoE rings + Migkas A(ell) extrema loops in the Galactic frame.

Concept:
  Pure CoE axisymmetry → constant A on small-circle rings about x = CoE↔anti-CoE.
  Scan A vs angle from +x (anti-CoE) around 360°. After-2ℓ A(ℓ) has TWO maxima
  and TWO minima (from best_fit_2ell_multiplier.npz A_after):
    MAX at ℓ = 30° and 185° from +x,
    MIN at ℓ = 115° and 265° from +x.

  Four widened loops (half-width ±18°, matching Amp×sin ±5% ranges):
    MAX: 30±18 → [12°, 48°] and 185±18 → [167°, 203°]
    MIN: 115±18 → [97°, 133°] and 265±18 → [247°, 283°]
  Each loop = two boundary small-circles + light fill between (μ-space),
  NOT giant filled sky caps. 283° is simply the outer edge of MIN 265±18
  (no separate decorative companion).

  Galactic orientation: anti-CoE (+x) at ℓ=0°, b=0°; CoE (−x) at ℓ=180°, b=0°.
  Sky markers (ℓ, b):
    Maxes: map extrema (17°, −9°) for ~30° max; strip (185°, 0°) for second max.
    Mins:  strip (115°, 0°) for ~115° min; map extrema (274°, −22°) for ~265° min.

Outputs:
  coe_rings_migkas_pin_axis.png
  coe_rings_migkas_pin_axis.json
"""

